---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Experience" description="Darshan Kansara's progression from infrastructure and datacenter operations to cloud, data platforms, and applied AI.">
    <header class="experience-hero">
      <div class="experience-title"><p class="eyebrow">Experience</p><h1>Learn the system.<br />Then make it simpler.</h1></div>
      <div class="experience-summary">
        <p class="intro">{site.yearsExperience} years across infrastructure, cloud, and data platforms. The roles changed. The work kept returning to the same question: how can a complex system become easier to understand and improve?</p>
        <div class="hero-facts" aria-label="Career facts">
          <div><strong>{site.yearsAtMicrosoft}</strong><span>years at Microsoft</span></div>
          <div><strong>$1M+</strong><span>annual platform savings</span></div>
          <div><strong>1998</strong><span>hands-on beginning</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="chapter current">
      <div class="chapter-meta"><span>2022—Today</span><span>Microsoft</span></div>
      <div class="chapter-copy">
        <p class="role">Senior Manager · Platform Reliability &amp; Operations</p>
        <h2>Operating the data platform as a product.</h2>
        <p>Leading reliability, security, infrastructure, continuity, and cost discipline for a business-critical cloud marketing data platform built on Azure services including Synapse, Cosmos DB, and Fabric.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>$1M+ platform spend reduction</strong><span>Capacity optimization, automation, and removal of recurring inefficiency.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Stronger operating signals</strong><span>Clearer monitoring, incident response, and readiness practices across the platform.</span></li>
          <li><strong>Shared accountability</strong><span>Engineering, privacy, security, compliance, and operations working against one system view.</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-meta"><span>2020—2022</span><span>Microsoft</span></div>
      <div class="chapter-copy">
        <p class="role">Senior Program Manager · Cloud Operations &amp; Continuous Improvement</p>
        <h2>Turning capacity pressure into an improvement system.</h2>
        <p>Connected demand forecasting, spares planning, finance, and supply-chain decisions so teams could see cost and operational risk earlier. Lean and Kaizen methods became practical tools for removing delay and repeated work, not presentation language.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-meta"><span>2011—2020</span><span>Microsoft</span></div>
      <div class="chapter-copy">
        <p class="role">Datacenter Strategy, Automation &amp; Reliability Leadership</p>
        <h2>Making cloud infrastructure safer to change.</h2>
        <p>Worked across Azure datacenter tooling, critical-environment IT, automation, and global operations as cloud scale accelerated. Established the first Azure Datacenter Instrumentation &amp; Pre-Production Lab so infrastructure changes could be tested before broad rollout.</p>
        <blockquote>Reliability improved when uncertainty moved out of production and into a place designed for learning.</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter">
      <div class="chapter-meta"><span>2005—2011</span><span>TCS · Microsoft engagement</span></div>
      <div class="chapter-copy">
        <p class="role">Service Delivery &amp; IT Operations</p>
        <h2>Learning consequence through customer-facing services.</h2>
        <p>Owned service delivery and datacenter operations for Microsoft online services across India and Redmond. Availability, incident response, and service-level commitments made the relationship between technical choices and customer experience impossible to ignore.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="chapter foundation">
      <div class="chapter-meta"><span>1998—2005</span><span>India</span></div>
      <div class="chapter-copy">
        <p class="role">Infrastructure &amp; Networking</p>
        <h2>The foundation was physical.</h2>
        <p>Servers, networks, operating systems, and the hands-on work beneath the service. That proximity to the machine shaped an enduring preference: understand what the abstraction is hiding before deciding how to improve it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="credentials">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Credentials</p><h2>Formal learning, kept in proportion.</h2></div>
      <div class="credential-copy">
        <p><strong>PMP · PMI-ACP · ITIL v3 · CDCP · CDCS</strong><br />Program leadership, agile practice, service management, and datacenter disciplines.</p>
        <p><strong>MCSE · CCNA · HP PSE · CNE</strong><br />The infrastructure and networking foundation.</p>
        <p><strong>Post Graduate Diploma in Information Technology</strong><br />Sikkim Manipal University, India</p>
        <p><strong>Diploma in Computer Engineering</strong><br />Gujarat State Technical Board, India</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing">
      <p class="eyebrow">What the timeline leaves behind</p>
      <h2>The work is not a list of roles. It is a widening view of the system.</h2>
      <div><a href="/impact">See the evidence <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a><a href="/projects">See what I build <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></div>
    </section>
  <style>
    main{background:var(--paper)}
    .experience-hero{padding:clamp(72px,9vw,110px) max(var(--pad),calc((100vw - var(--max))/2));background:var(--ink);color:#fff;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:clamp(48px,8vw,120px);align-items:end}.eyebrow{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.68rem;letter-spacing:.15em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#7ebaff}.experience-hero h1{font-size:clamp(3.2rem,5.5vw,5.4rem);line-height:.96;letter-spacing:-.04em;color:#fff;max-width:12ch;margin-top:26px}.intro{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(1.08rem,1.7vw,1.3rem);line-height:1.55;color:#b9c6d7;max-width:620px}.hero-facts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-top:44px;border-top:1px solid var(--line-dark)}.hero-facts div{padding:20px 16px 0 0;display:grid;gap:5px}.hero-facts strong{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.55rem;line-height:1}.hero-facts span{font-size:.7rem;color:#8796aa;max-width:15ch}
    .chapter{width:min(var(--max),calc(100% - 2 * var(--pad)));margin:auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:190px 1fr;gap:clamp(34px,7vw,96px);padding:clamp(62px,7vw,86px) 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.chapter-meta{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:7px;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.65rem;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--muted)}.chapter-meta span:first-child{color:var(--azure)}.chapter-copy{max-width:820px}.role{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:.66rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#86662a}.chapter h2,.credentials h2,.closing h2{font-size:clamp(1.9rem,3.4vw,3.15rem);line-height:1.06;letter-spacing:-.03em;margin:18px 0 24px}.chapter-copy>p:last-of-type{font-size:1.02rem;color:var(--muted);max-width:67ch}.chapter ul{list-style:none;margin:36px 0 0;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.chapter li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(180px,.75fr) 1.25fr;gap:28px;padding:18px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.chapter li span{color:var(--muted);font-size:.88rem}.chapter blockquote{margin:34px 0 0;padding:0 0 0 24px;border-left:2px solid var(--azure);font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(1.25rem,2vw,1.65rem);line-height:1.4;color:#2f5c96;max-width:28ch}.foundation{border-bottom:0}
    .credentials{padding:clamp(68px,8vw,96px) var(--pad);background:var(--white);display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(260px,.8fr) 1.2fr;gap:clamp(44px,8vw,110px)}.credentials>div{max-width:650px}.credentials .eyebrow{color:#916d2c}.credentials h2{margin-bottom:0}.credential-copy p{padding:18px 0;margin:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);color:var(--muted)}.credential-copy p:last-child{border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.credential-copy strong{color:var(--text)}
    .closing{padding:clamp(72px,8vw,98px) var(--pad);background:#10233e;color:#fff}.closing>*{width:min(var(--max),100%);margin-left:auto;margin-right:auto}.closing h2{color:#fff;max-width:20ch}.closing div{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px;margin-top:32px}.closing a{padding:13px 18px;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.24);color:#fff;font-weight:600}.closing a:first-child{background:#fff;color:var(--ink)}
    @media(max-width:760px){.experience-hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;padding-top:54px;padding-bottom:58px;gap:30px}.experience-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.75rem,12vw,3.7rem);margin-top:20px}.intro{font-size:1rem}.hero-facts{margin-top:28px}.chapter{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.chapter-meta{flex-direction:row;justify-content:space-between}.chapter li{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:7px}.credentials{grid-template-columns:1fr}.closing div{flex-direction:column}.closing a{text-align:center}}
  </style>
  <style>
    :global(body),main{background:var(--ink);color:var(--text)}
    .experience-hero{min-height:68vh;background:transparent;color:var(--text);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);align-items:end}
    .eyebrow{color:var(--gold);letter-spacing:.08em}.experience-hero h1{color:var(--paper);font-size:clamp(3.4rem,6.8vw,6.8rem);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0;line-height:.88}
    .intro{font-family:var(--font-sans);color:var(--muted);font-size:clamp(1rem,1.5vw,1.2rem)}
    .hero-facts{border-color:var(--line)}.hero-facts strong{color:var(--paper);font-weight:400}.hero-facts span{color:var(--dim)}
    .chapter{position:relative;grid-template-columns:var(--rail) 1fr;border-color:var(--line);padding:clamp(66px,8vw,108px) 0}
    .chapter::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:calc(var(--rail) + (var(--gutter) / 2));top:0;bottom:0;width:1px;background:var(--line)}
    .chapter-meta{position:relative;color:var(--dim);letter-spacing:.06em}.chapter-meta::after{content:"";position:absolute;top:8px;right:calc(var(--gutter) / -2 - 4px);width:7px;height:7px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ink);border:1px solid var(--gold)}.chapter-meta span:first-child{color:var(--gold)}
    .role{color:var(--azure);letter-spacing:.06em}.chapter h2,.credentials h2,.closing h2{color:var(--paper);font-weight:400;letter-spacing:0}
    .chapter-copy>p:last-of-type,.chapter li span{color:var(--muted)}.chapter ul,.chapter li{border-color:var(--line)}.chapter blockquote{color:var(--azure-bright);border-color:var(--azure);font-weight:400}
    .credentials,.closing{background:transparent;color:var(--text);border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
    .credentials{grid-template-columns:var(--rail) 1fr}.credentials .eyebrow{color:var(--gold)}.credential-copy p{border-color:var(--line);color:var(--muted)}.credential-copy strong{color:var(--paper)}
    .closing h2{color:var(--paper)}.closing a{border-color:var(--line);color:var(--paper);font-weight:500}.closing a:first-child{background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink)}
    @media(max-width:760px){.chapter::before,.chapter-meta::after{display:none}.experience-hero{min-height:auto}.credentials{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
  </style>
</Base>
